<cell id="a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000010"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## Backtest — Inference on Out-of-Sample Data

Run the trained agent in **pure greedy mode (epsilon=0, no exploration, no training)** over a date range the agent has never seen.

**Instructions:**
1. Make sure training is complete and `eurusd_gpu_ph7_final.pt` exists in your Drive checkpoints folder
2. Set `date_from` / `date_to` to a period **outside** your training range (`2021-01-01` to `2023-12-31`)
3. Run the cell — it walks through every bar in the date range sequentially and logs each day's result
4. Results include: pass rate, average daily return, max drawdown, total return, Sharpe ratio, final equity
5. Optionally save daily results to a CSV for further analysis

**What the output means:**
- `PASS` — daily return >= 2.5% AND drawdown <= 1% (FTMO target hit)
- `OK`   — positive return AND drawdown <= 1% (profitable but below target)
- `FAIL` — negative return OR drawdown > 1%
- `pass_rate_pct` — % of days the agent hit the FTMO daily target
- `max_dd_overall_pct` — worst peak-to-trough drawdown across the entire backtest period
- `sharpe_ratio` — annualised Sharpe using daily returns (>1.0 is good, >2.0 is strong)</cell id="a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000010">
<cell id="a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000011">from gpu_rl_trading.eval.backtest import run_backtest

CHECKPOINT = "/content/drive/MyDrive/gpu_rl_trading/checkpoints/eurusd_gpu_ph7_final.pt"

results = run_backtest(
    checkpoint_path = CHECKPOINT,
    csv_path        = DATA_CSV_EURUSD,
    date_from       = "2024-01-01",   # must be AFTER your training end date (2023-12-31)
    date_to         = "2024-12-31",
    out_csv         = "/content/drive/MyDrive/gpu_rl_trading/metrics/backtest_2024.csv",
)

# results["metrics"]     — summary dict
# results["daily_df"]    — per-day DataFrame
# results["equity_curve"]— list of per-bar equity values
# results["action_log"]  — list of per-bar actions (0=FLAT, 1-3=BUY, 4-6=SELL)</cell id="a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000011">
<cell id="a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000012"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>### Plot Equity Curve</cell id="a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000012">
<cell id="a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000013">import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import numpy as np

equity = np.array(results["equity_curve"])
daily_df = results["daily_df"]
metrics  = results["metrics"]

fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 1, figsize=(14, 10))

# Equity curve
axes[0].plot(equity, color="royalblue", linewidth=0.8)
axes[0].axhline(100_000, color="gray", linestyle="--", linewidth=0.6)
axes[0].set_title(f"Equity Curve  |  Final: ${metrics['final_equity']:,.0f}  "
                  f"Total Return: {metrics['total_return_pct']:+.2f}%")
axes[0].set_ylabel("Equity ($)")
axes[0].grid(True, alpha=0.3)

# Drawdown
peak = np.maximum.accumulate(equity)
dd   = (peak - equity) / (peak + 1e-8) * 100
axes[1].fill_between(range(len(dd)), dd, color="tomato", alpha=0.6)
axes[1].set_title(f"Drawdown  |  Max: {metrics['max_dd_overall_pct']:.2f}%")
axes[1].set_ylabel("Drawdown (%)")
axes[1].grid(True, alpha=0.3)

# Daily FTMO flags
if len(daily_df) > 0:
    colors = {"PASS": "green", "OK": "gold", "FAIL": "red"}
    bar_colors = [colors[f] for f in daily_df["ftmo_flag"]]
    axes[2].bar(range(len(daily_df)), daily_df["daily_return_pct"],
                color=bar_colors, alpha=0.8, width=0.8)
    axes[2].axhline(0, color="black", linewidth=0.5)
    axes[2].set_title(
        f"Daily Returns  |  PASS={metrics['pass_days']} ({metrics['pass_rate_pct']}%)  "
        f"OK={metrics['ok_days']}  FAIL={metrics['fail_days']}  "
        f"Sharpe={metrics['sharpe_ratio']:.2f}")
    axes[2].set_ylabel("Daily Return (%)")
    axes[2].set_xlabel("Trading Day")
    axes[2].grid(True, alpha=0.3)

plt.tight_layout()
plt.savefig("/content/drive/MyDrive/gpu_rl_trading/metrics/backtest_equity_curve.png",
            dpi=150, bbox_inches="tight")
plt.show()
print("Chart saved to Drive.")</cell id="a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000013">
